This is an example where the argument is only known approximately. The question arises as t how many decimal places one should retain 1 P(x). If \Delta x and \Delta P(x) denote the error in x an the resulting error in P(x), respectively, then
\Delta P(x)\approx Z(x)\Delta x
Hence \Delta P(1.960)=3\times10^{-4} which indicates the P(1.960) need only be calculated to 4D. There fore P(1.960)=.9750.
